#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073563 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073881 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "48f71a07-2bd3-5164-a227-b82d56c0abc7" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Ratio to Compute a Denominator"}] :question/id #uuid "913c1995-fe26-5359-8298-e3b8379e39d8" :question/math-academy-id "e-2277" :question/problem "In Jennifer's garden, there are $60$ roses. The ratio of roses to orchids is $\\dfrac{3}{5}$. How many orchids are there in the garden?" :question/worked-solution "The ratio of roses to orchids is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of roses and the denominator represents the number of orchids.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $60$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $20$:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}3}\\times 20}{{\\color{red}5}\\times 20} = \\dfrac{{\\color{blue}60}}{{\\color{red}100}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in Jennifer's garden, there are $100$ orchids."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073564 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073882 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d710628f-14e0-5587-90d1-564a5e0ead19" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Ratio to Compute a Numerator"}] :question/id #uuid "2eeba279-cd91-55c7-b423-a14edb255ebb" :question/math-academy-id "e-2278" :question/problem "The ratio of sand to crushed stone in concrete is $\\dfrac{3}{2}$. If Daniel has $80$ kilograms of crushed stone available to make concrete, what amount of sand should he use?" :question/worked-solution "We are given that the ratio of sand to crushed stone in concrete is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{2}\n$$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the amount of sand and the denominator represents the amount of crushed stone.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $80$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $40$:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{{\\color{blue}3}\\times 40}{{\\color{red}2}\\times 40} = \\dfrac{{\\color{blue}120}}{{\\color{red}80}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for $80$ kilograms of crushed stone, Daniel must use $120$ kilograms of sand."}]}
